If you like relaxing while you play;
If you like gathering / crafting / building base;
If you like exploring, then this game is for you.
Low Price, little game that last for many hours, with random gen map. You can farm, tame animals, kill some goblin and probably many more beast (im not far enough in the game yet to know)
Many things to do in this great game. For me, it worth the money and even more... I hope to get some more update or DLC.

At this moment in time I wouldn't recommend this game. It has a lot of bugs at the moments; like when you select rematch sometimes it chooses not to work and you have to exit to the main menu and try again. The timer before your car explodes is too short, you either die immediately or have to go so fast that the other player can't place objects in an effective manner.
TLDR;
Buggy and just not fun atm.

The game is firmly "meh".
- It's pretty, following Blizzard's art style;
- It tries to be funny, but isn't;
- The gameplay is not overly engaging, nor exciting;
- The missions quickly feel repetative;
- The skill trees are not inspiring. They don't add much to the repetative combat;
- The upgrades are all about enabling more upgrades, not changing the game play.

Valve made ​​a documentary about professional players Dota 2 , their participation in the world championship , simultaneously revealing them as real people with their own thoughts , desires, feelings. When finished viewing the film left behind a dual experience.
On the one hand , rarely make films of this kind ( the more so qualitatively ) - because not everyone is interested to see how young people play games at the championships , but great direction, sound and , more importantly, a beautiful installation , make this movie fun for all , allowing look behind the scenes of eSports . Well in the film shows the relationship of players and their families to the games , as well shown related to eSports in different countries - somewhere they are popular players around them cares . And most importantly - the players are shown and as gamers and as people , for some games , a way to escape from stress, someone wants fame , and some hope that his ex- girl looks at his game in the championship. This approach unwittingly imbued with sympathy for the players .
On the other hand, the apparent non-intrusive and very tactful propaganda infusion eSports :
Yes, extremely high barrier to entry for this week you will have to sacrifice important examinations and relaxed family atmosphere , and still possible relationship with his girlfriend ;
Yes, one point in the championship can solve everything, and if an error occurs because of this moment may scoff at you for a long time all over the Internet ;
Yes, after 25 years, you definitely leave for retirement - you will have a reaction is not the same ;
- What do you do after 25 , not having behind nothing but the ability to play like a pro in one game - not our problem ;
- At the end of the film we " optimistic " assure that future professional players are popular players and Olympic champions . Given that Valve removed this film , considering that Valve created Dota 2 , it becomes clear that these words are more publicity future plans of the company * joke about anything, but not Half-Life 3 . Like it or not , but at the moment , many more know Cristiano Ronaldo and Messi than Tail and Dandy . Good or bad - I do not know , wait and see .
